puddle doctor (puddle 0.1.0, linux x86_64)

ok    CPU virtualization  on (the hypervisor uses it)
ok    Hypervisor          /dev/kvm is usable
ok    Bundled runtime     msb 0.7.7-puddle.2 (/opt/puddle/runtime/msb)
ok    Runtime starts      msb 0.7.7-puddle.2 (0.0 s)
ok    Test boot           a test VM booted and ran a program in 1.1 s
ok    Disk space          120 GB free on the drive that holds Puddle's data (/home/dev/.local/share/puddle)
FAIL  Data folder path    /Users/dev/Library/Application Support has an ACL entry that lets another account change it (group:everyone allow add_file,delete_child), so msb will not open Puddle's data below it
      impact: Puddle can't start any workspace: another account may change a folder above its
              data.
      remedy: Remove that account's access entry, or keep Puddle's data under a folder only you
              can enter.
      fix:    msb refuses a folder where another account holds an ACL entry that can add, delete
              or change things. If you added the entry, remove it with `chmod -a# 1
              '/Users/dev/Library/Application Support'` (`sudo` in front when you do not own the
              folder); otherwise keep Puddle's data under a folder only you can enter, or ask
              whoever manages this Mac.
      from:   /Users/dev/Library/Application Support ACL entry 1: group:everyone allow
              add_file,delete_child
ok    Disk encryption     data drive encrypted (BitLocker); swap /dev/dm-1 encrypted (BitLocker)
ok    SSH agent           the agent on /run/user/1000/agent.sock holds 1 key (ed25519: 1)
ok    Azure CLI (az)      version 2.64.0
ok    Credential store    the operating system's credential store: a test write and delete worked

1 problem to fix before Puddle can run sandboxes. (1.2 s)

